IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cccfa-types`

-- Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 — GOAL 4: STATUTORY
-- DAMAGES.
--
--   "How much statutory damages does a breach give the debtor?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_52.txt — s 89.

§ `Goal 4 — statutory damages`

-- s 89 "(1) The amount of the statutory damages is,— [for s 9C(3)(a)] an
-- amount equal to the interest charges, credit fees, and default fees that
-- have become payable ...; [s 9C(4)(a)] the amount paid by the guarantor ...;
-- [s 9C(5)(a)] the amount paid by the borrower ...; [s 45F or 45G] ... the
-- interest charges, credit fees, and default fees that have become payable
-- ...; [s 18] ... payable ... during the period to which the breach relates;
-- [s 24] ... payable ... during the period [of the request] ...; [s 25(1)(a)]
-- the lesser of $6,000 or 5% of the total of all advances ...; in the case of
-- any other breach, the lesser of $6,000 or 5% of,— [the credit limit, cash
-- price, total advances or rateable value] (1A) ... if a revolving credit
-- contract does not have a credit limit, the amount of the statutory damages
-- is $6,000. (2) If the amount of the statutory damages under subsection
-- (1)(d) is less than $200, [it] must be rounded up to $200." With the labels
-- lost, (1)(d) is read as the "any other breach" limb (fork F5).
@ref s 89(1)-(2)
GIVEN b IS A Breach
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory damages for` b MEANS
    CONSIDER b's `kind of breach`
    WHEN `s 25(1)(a) disclosure of a guarantee` THEN min 6000 (0.05 TIMES b's `amount measured`)
    WHEN `any other breach` THEN
        IF   b's `kind of contract` EQUALS `a revolving credit contract` AND b's `a revolving contract without a credit limit`
        THEN 6000
        ELSE max 200 (min 6000 (0.05 TIMES b's `amount measured`))
    OTHERWISE b's `amount measured`

-- s 89 "(3) If a person has breached 2 or more provisions ... in connection
-- with the same ... contract ... and the breaches occur at or about the same
-- time, the total statutory damages payable for those breaches is equal to
-- the highest statutory damages payable for 1 of those breaches."
@ref s 89(3)
@export The statutory damages for breaches of the Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 (NZ) at or about the same time on one contract, under s 89: the highest of the amounts for each breach — the interest and fees payable for lender responsibility, high-cost and disclosure breaches, the amount paid for guarantor and insurance breaches, and otherwise the lesser of $6,000 and 5% of the credit limit or advances (at least $200; $6,000 for revolving credit without a limit). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN breaches IS A LIST OF Breach  @desc The breaches at or about the same time, each with its kind, the kind of contract, and the amount s 89 measures
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the statutory damages for the simultaneous breaches` breaches MEANS
    IF   null breaches
    THEN 0
    ELSE maximum (map (GIVEN b YIELD `the statutory damages for` b) breaches)
